<pending_commit branch="chromeos-3.18" change_id="I553906ed18f8d896a2167ebdbc0e266e5feb5c66" commit="9ad0f700c0aea288e5757fec69d6577d1bdee1d9" commit_message="CHROMIUM: ARM64: dragon: enable CONFIG_ERROR_ON_WARNING  BUG=chromium:534254 TEST=emerge-smaug chromeos-kernel-3_18  Change-Id: I553906ed18f8d896a2167ebdbc0e266e5feb5c66 Signed-off-by: Nicolas Boichat &lt;drinkcat@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/300948 Reviewed-by: Olof Johansson &lt;olofj@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="300948" owner_email="drinkcat@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="6" project="chromiumos/third_party/kernel" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/third_party/kernel" ref="refs/changes/48/300948/6" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="I9a9f64c14ad015e21d08eec36e8fc187189cd2f2" commit="4bf1173acd7deb68d82982620d0a9e2b7fcedc3a" commit_message="Add NV flag to default boot legacy OS  In developer mode, this option will make the system try to boot into a legacy OS first after the 30 second timeout. This removes the need to press a key during boot to try legacy mode and the need to remove the write protect screw to boot legacy as default.  BUG=chromium:310697 BRANCH=none TEST=make runtests  Change-Id: I9a9f64c14ad015e21d08eec36e8fc187189cd2f2 Signed-off-by: Mary Ruthven &lt;mruthven@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/304077 Reviewed-by: Randall Spangler &lt;rspangler@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="304077" owner_email="mruthven@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="12" project="chromiumos/platform/vboot_reference" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/platform/vboot_reference" ref="refs/changes/77/304077/12" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="I9134bcda7741eee7fdf41b1088272abf74d2e112" commit="dfd9e94e37f39bba4e6b1af27cf650d1f351f98d" commit_message="buffet: Remove buffet_test_daemon  BUG=none TEST=none  Change-Id: I9134bcda7741eee7fdf41b1088272abf74d2e112 Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/305462 Commit-Ready: Vitaly Buka &lt;vitalybuka@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: Vitaly Buka &lt;vitalybuka@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Alex Vakulenko &lt;avakulenko@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="305462" owner_email="vitalybuka@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="1" project="chromiumos/platform2" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/platform2" ref="refs/changes/62/305462/1" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="chromeos-3.18" change_id="I1f3f3d4eb3dd93e926234739070022dd95dfe149" commit="d75797d0a844d8f387974e49c1ec48a7395c3036" commit_message="FROMLIST: genirq: Allow migration of chained interrupts by installing default action  When a CPU is offlined all interrupts that have an action are migrated to other still online CPUs. However, if the interrupt has chained handler installed this is not done. Chained handlers are used by GPIO drivers which support interrupts, for instance.  When the affinity is not corrected properly we end up in situation where most interrupts are not arriving to the online CPUs anymore. For example on Intel Braswell system which has SD-card card detection signal connected to a GPIO the IO-APIC routing entries look like below after CPU1 is offlined:    pin30, enabled , level, low , V(52), IRR(0), S(0), logical , D(03), M(1)   pin31, enabled , level, low , V(42), IRR(0), S(0), logical , D(03), M(1)   pin32, enabled , level, low , V(62), IRR(0), S(0), logical , D(03), M(1)   pin5b, enabled , level, low , V(72), IRR(0), S(0), logical , D(03), M(1)  The problem here is that the destination mask still contains both CPUs even if CPU1 is already offline. This means that the IO-APIC still routes interrupts to the other CPU as well.  We solve the problem by providing a default action for chained interrupts. This action allows the migration code to correct affinity (as it finds desc-&gt;action != NULL).  Also make the default action handler to emit a warning if for some reason a chained handler ends up calling it.  Signed-off-by: Mika Westerberg &lt;mika.westerberg@linux.intel.com&gt; (am from https://patchwork.kernel.org/patch/7325891) Signed-off-by: U. Artie Eoff &lt;ullysses.a.eoff@intel.com&gt;  BUG=chrome-os-partner:45628 TEST=`echo 0 &gt; /sys/devices/system/cpu/cpu1/online`      Verify input devices continue to respond to user      input.  Change-Id: I1f3f3d4eb3dd93e926234739070022dd95dfe149 Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/301592 Commit-Ready: Ullysses A Eoff &lt;ullysses.a.eoff@intel.com&gt; Tested-by: Russ Sage &lt;russ.sage@intel.com&gt; Reviewed-by: Bernie Thompson &lt;bhthompson@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Eric Caruso &lt;ejcaruso@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Ganesh R Patil &lt;ganesh.r.patil@intel.com&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="301592" owner_email="ullysses.a.eoff@intel.com" pass_count="0" patch_number="3" project="chromiumos/third_party/kernel" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/third_party/kernel" ref="refs/changes/92/301592/3" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="Ie50a499a3f2fc52089446c214949541a7b2b6436" commit="dd058f2e77df4149a6a0e22aa2059a0bfff5f104" commit_message="baseboard-kunimitsu: add disk_layout.json  All Kunimitsu systems should use an eMMC so we need to point at it.  BUG=chrome-os-partner:46046 TEST=None  Change-Id: Ie50a499a3f2fc52089446c214949541a7b2b6436 Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/305217 Commit-Ready: Bernie Thompson &lt;bhthompson@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: Bernie Thompson &lt;bhthompson@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Duncan Laurie &lt;dlaurie@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="305217" owner_email="bhthompson@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="1" project="chromiumos/overlays/board-overlays" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/overlays/board-overlays" ref="refs/changes/17/305217/1" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="I9180eb85b0b2a7e0b137e6c5218c77b334f1f163" commit="cdb741529f0a8aad5db96a591e451392badf0376" commit_message="Add veyron_minnie-cheets canary builder  BUG=chromium:538232 TEST=None  Change-Id: I9180eb85b0b2a7e0b137e6c5218c77b334f1f163 Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/303434 Commit-Ready: Bernie Thompson &lt;bhthompson@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: Bernie Thompson &lt;bhthompson@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Bernie Thompson &lt;bhthompson@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="303434" owner_email="bhthompson@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="3" project="chromiumos/chromite" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/chromite" ref="refs/changes/34/303434/3" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="chromeos-3.8" change_id="I1156032c9f2c36c28b0baea0f38ce985788701f7" commit="71c4d153b0414823c168ea3d85d77ff0d7a94412" commit_message="Revert &quot;BACKPORT: HID: multitouch: Fix fields from pen report ID being interpreted for multitouch&quot;  Caused regression where Dell P2314T &amp; Smart board 8055i stop working.  BUG=chromium:539335  This reverts commit 8a1c7c3381d853a226728059b6cf0efc52cff7f7.  Change-Id: I1156032c9f2c36c28b0baea0f38ce985788701f7 Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/305441 Commit-Ready: Michael Spang &lt;spang@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: Michael Spang &lt;spang@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Michael Spang &lt;spang@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="305441" owner_email="spang@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="1" project="chromiumos/third_party/kernel" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/third_party/kernel" ref="refs/changes/41/305441/1" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="